  "summary": "FIT inverters run paired fault codes: the E-code (E13, E15, E21...) is the critical shutdown, and a plain-number twin (14, 16, 54...) means the same condition is happening 'frequently' but the control decided it can keep running. Those numbers are your early warning — the cheapest repair happens before the E-code lockout.",
