  "summary": "The unit gets a call but the compressor never starts, and there is no separate contactor to check because the compressor relay is built into the unitary (UC) control board. You test it by measuring voltage across the on-board relay contacts with the call active. The UC control also has a built-in short cycle delay that will fool you if you measure too soon.",
