  "summary": "A tripped fuse, breaker, or ground fault device is strong evidence of a real electrical fault, not a nuisance. This test finds a grounded compressor without pulling the terminal cover until you have to, and it explains why a megohmmeter reading alone should not condemn a scroll.",
