   "Read the Maximum Allowable Pressure from the serial plate and pressurize to that value for step 3, holding 1 hour (4 hours recommended). Take extreme care not to over-pressurize.",
   "Apply the correct minimum test pressures: the low side minimum is the low side Maximum Allowable Pressure and the high side minimum is the high side Maximum Allowable Pressure.",
   "If the high side cannot be isolated from the low side, test the entire system to the low side Maximum Allowable Pressure instead.",
   "Repeat the full pressure test after any repair, and proceed to evacuation only when no leaks exist.",
   "Evacuate with a 250 micron capable pump to 500 microns or less using both the suction and liquid service valves, then close the pump valve and hold 10 minutes to confirm the vacuum holds steady.",
