   "With power supplied, perform the compressor diode check on the back of the inverter PCB: diode voltage from U(24), V(25), W(26) to P(27), and from N(23-21) to U(24), V(25), W(26), should each read 0.3 to 0.7 V.",
   "Perform the resistance check across those same point pairs - each should read more than 500k.",
   "Replace the inverter PCB if any reading is out of range.",
   "For the DC link voltage test, disconnect power to the unit for 15 to 20 minutes so the bus capacitors discharge.",
   "Locate the fan motor plug, note the red and black wire pin locations, and disconnect the plug.",
   "Resupply power, measure incoming line voltage, and multiply it by 1.41 - that product is the DC voltage you should read.",
   "Note that test point locations vary from model to model, so verify the points against documentation for the exact model before condemning the board."
