   "Start the system and place a piece of cardboard in front of the condenser coil to raise condensing pressure.",
   "Note the pressure at which the control cuts out. A cutout at 610 PSIG plus or minus 10 PSIG is normal operation.",
   "If it cuts out below that range, replace the control. If it cuts out in range, the high head pressure is real - work the causes of high head pressure instead.",
   "Remove the cardboard immediately after the test and confirm the control resets automatically as pressure falls."
