  "title": "Carrier 24VNA9/25VNA8 - the UI defrost setting supersedes the outdoor board DIP switches",
  "summary": "The heat pump defrosts too often or not often enough and the DIP switches on the outdoor board look right. On these units the user interface setting supersedes the control board DIP switch settings when the two disagree; the DIP switches only govern with a non-communicating thermostat.",
  "steps": [
   "Determine whether the system runs a communicating user interface or a non-communicating thermostat - this decides which setting is actually in control.",
   "On a communicating system, read and change the defrost interval at the UI, since the UI setting supersedes the DIP switch settings on the control board if they are not the same.",
   "With a non-communicating thermostat, set the defrost interval using the dip switches on the outdoor control board per the legend for that board (the manual shows separate figures for the 1 and 2 ton AOC board and the 3, 4 and 5 ton board).",
   "If AUTO is selected, expect the interval to float: after a defrost shorter than 5 minutes the next interval is 90 minutes, 5 to 7 minutes gives 60 minutes, and longer than 7 minutes gives 30 minutes.",
   "Remember the first interval after any power up defaults to 30 minutes, with remaining intervals at the selected time - do not read that as a fault.",
   "Confirm a defrost demand actually exists: coil temperature must be at or below 32F for 4 minutes during the interval, and defrost is only allowed below 50F outdoor ambient.",
   "If the coil never reaches 32F within the interval, the interval timer resets and starts over - that is normal control logic, not a stuck timer."
  ],
  "confidence": "verify"
