  "title": "Burning inside the burner venturi - telling flashback and extinction pop from delayed ignition",
  "summary": "You find flame burning back inside the burner venturi. Delayed ignition and flashback both produce this, but flashback is the burning speed exceeding the gas-air velocity leaving the burner port, and the two have different fixes, so identify which one you have before repairing.",
