   "Disconnect the DC link voltage connector from the FAN PCB, leaving it connected at the Inverter PCB.",
   "Move the disconnected end of the DC link harness to a safe location so voltage can be read from White to Yellow with power applied.",
   "Restore power and check DC link voltage at that harness.",
   "If supply power, EMI fuses and the reactor all test in range but DC link voltage is under 150 VDC, replace Inverter 1 and the Fan PCB; if DC link voltage is accurate, replace Inverter #1 PCB.",
   "Leave the unit powered off 15 to 20 minutes again before reconnecting any wire harness or the DC link connector."
