  "summary": "Inverter outdoor units hold a stored DC charge after the disconnect is pulled. Lennox mini-split procedures call for a minimum of 15 minutes powered off before disconnecting comm wires or boards, and 15 to 20 minutes on the 460V heat pump and heat recovery units before reconnecting harnesses or the DC link.",
