   "Set all zone thermostats to fan AUTO and see whether the complaint goes away over a day or two.",
   "Check the panel's purge or blower-off delay setting - a long post-cycle blower run pushes residual conditioned air into satisfied zones the same way.",
   "Verify closed dampers are actually closing and sealing, since a leaky closed damper produces the same complaint even on AUTO.",
   "Confirm the system is not running a bypass damper wide open, which recirculates supply air and worsens temperature drift.",
   "If the customer genuinely needs circulation, look at whether the panel supports a timed circulate mode instead of continuous fan, and set expectations about zone drift."
