  "title": "Cold climate vapor injection (EVI) heat pump - what the extra circuit changes at service",
  "summary": "Vapor injection heat pumps split part of the liquid flow through a second expansion device and a heat exchanger, then inject that cooled vapor into the middle of the compression process. That extra circuit gives capacity and keeps the compressor cooler at low outdoor temperatures, but it also means there are readings and components on the unit that a conventional heat pump does not have. Do not diagnose one by conventional superheat and subcooling alone.",
