  "summary": "Subcooling read at the outdoor service valve tells you what is leaving the condenser, not what is arriving at the metering device. On a long line set, an undersized liquid line, or a run with significant vertical lift up to an attic air handler, the liquid can lose enough pressure on the way that it flashes before it gets to the valve. The gauge at the condenser looks acceptable while the coil is being fed vapor.",
