  "summary": "Refrigerant-side numbers tell you the circuit is behaving, not that the equipment is delivering its rated capacity. Measuring the change in air enthalpy across the evaporator, combined with airflow, gives you the actual heat being removed - and it catches the latent side that a dry bulb temperature split misses. Wet bulb tracks enthalpy closely enough that techs use it as a proxy in the field.",
