  "summary": "If air can go around the coil instead of through it, you get a low split with normal-looking static pressure, because bypassing air adds no resistance and no heat transfer. Gaps at the sides of a coil slab, a missing filler panel, an oversized cabinet or plenum, or an unsealed filter rack all do this. Rule it out before you go chasing the refrigerant side.",
