  "title": "Registers add up to far less air than the blower is supposed to be moving",
  "summary": "Hooding every supply and summing the readings is the honest check on a duct system. When the sum comes in well under what the blower table says the unit should deliver at the measured static, the missing air is either leaking out of the ducts, never being produced by the blower, or an artifact of how you took the readings.",
