  "summary": "The return air arriving at the equipment should be close to the air at the return grille. When it has shifted toward attic or crawlspace temperature by the time it reaches the unit, the return is drawing unconditioned air through leaks, and every capacity, split, and rise number you take downstream is corrupted. Three temperature readings separate this from a thermostat or stratification complaint.",
