  "id": "s-dual-cap-one-section-dead",
  "equipment": "Condenser/Heat Pump",
  "title": "Condenser fan spins fine but the compressor only hums - test each half of the dual capacitor separately",
  "summary": "A dual run capacitor is two independent sections sharing one common terminal. The FAN section can be at rating while the HERM section has lost most of its capacitance, so the fan runs normally and the compressor never gets the phase shift it needs to start. You have to read C to HERM and C to FAN as two separate tests. One good reading tells you nothing about the other half.",
