  "id": "s-24v-collapses-under-load",
  "equipment": "Condenser/Heat Pump",
  "title": "24V at the Y wire with it disconnected, but the contactor drops out the second you land it",
  "summary": "Open-circuit voltage tells you almost nothing. If there is extra resistance anywhere in the control circuit - a corroded splice, a nicked thermostat wire, an undersized long run, a burnt terminal - the voltage looks fine with the load off and collapses as soon as the contactor coil tries to draw current. The real test is voltage read across the coil while it is connected and calling.",
