  "summary": "On most residential equipment the transformer secondary common is bonded to the cabinet. That gives you a clean way to prove an open common conductor: R to chassis reads 24V while R to C reads nothing or an unstable number. If the common is broken anywhere between the transformer and the thermostat or an accessory, nothing operates even though voltage is clearly present.",
