  "summary": "On Mitsubishi M-series equipment the three-conductor run does two jobs at once. The installation literature gives S1 to S2 as the 208/230 VAC supply that feeds the indoor unit, and S2 to S3 as roughly 24 VDC carrying the serial signal. Taking both readings at the outdoor terminal block and then at the indoor terminal block splits the problem cleanly into supply, wiring, or board.",
